{"id": "9760d58a-7ec7-4e98-b306-0ced7bf741fd", "timestamp": "2026-10-22T18:42:53.956999", "source": "user", "parent_id": "ba6ee1c0-263d-487e-9de8-73b8fc033310", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"Bhai, design-only kaam hai — koi execution nahi. Pehle mujhe sirf teen cheezein chahiye, complete solution mat dena abhi: pehla, TorchOpt repo ka inspection — explicit gradient differentiation API kahan defined hai, kya signature hai (e.g., `torchopt.diff.implicit.meta_gradient_ad` ya functional/meta variants), kaise intermediate data reuse karta hai, aur memory allocation minimization ka mechanism kya hai (in-place updates, cached tensors, functional vs eager diff). Standard autograd comparison ke liye relevant PyTorch internals (torch.func, functorch transforms, vmap, grad) bhi note karo. Doosra, ek proposed approach — kaunse tasks/benchmarks choose karoge (e.g., bi-level optimization, hypergradient, implicit differentiation on a small NN), konsa TorchOpt API vs konsa PyTorch baseline, kaunse metrics (wall-clock per iteration, peak memory via torch.cuda.max_memory_allocated ya tracemalloc CPU par, numerical stability jaise gradient norm MSe ya final task loss drift across many seeds), aur kitne independent runs/seeds power ke liye. Teesra, consequential assumptions aur uncertainties — jaise TorchOpt API ko load karna possible hoga bina GPU ke (system Python, network disabled, deps not preinstalled), TorchOpt ka sahi entry point aur version availability, kya TorchOpt requires functorch which Torch ke alag version pin karta hai (compatibility assumption), kya fair comparison ke liye dono paths par identical mathematical formulation guarantee hoti hai ya sirf numeric approximation close hoti hai (yahi stability finding ko invalidate kar sakta hai), aur memory measurement methodology ka reproducibility (CPU-only tracing vs reported PyTorch sakes). Bas itna. Final design baad mein maangunga. Bas repo + approach + uncertainties return karo.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"plan\", \"approach_approved\": false, \"public_task\": {\"question\": \"Will the explicit gradient differentiation API in TorchOpt, which reuses intermediate data and minimizes memory allocation, reduce computation time and improve numerical stability compared to standard autograd implementations?\", \"context\": \"Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.\", \"environment\": {\"runtime\": \"bubblewrap\", \"network\": \"disabled\", \"repository\": \"/workspace\", \"python\": \"python3\", \"software_environment\": \"system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled\", \"datasets\": [], \"gpu_enabled\": false, \"cpu_affinity_count\": 24, \"note\": \"Successful exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment.\"}, \"researcher_topics\": [], \"question_budget\": 6, \"actor_step_budget\": 60, \"continue_after_initial_plan\": false}}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "kind": "MessageEvent", "source_event_index": 1}
